// Emberdown, read off its walls (NAR-15, docs/story/environment.md). The thing speaks, never a person; reading
// changes nothing. The catalog is `Dressing`.

title: Rest_Lintel
---
Lintel: Cut over a roost door, high on the cliff: "Land soft. Leave light." #still #line:0f55d73
Lintel: The ladder up to it is newer than the words. Its rungs are worn to the grain. #plant:5.6 #still #line:07a6f1a
===

title: Rest_TallyWall
---
Wall: A count for every year, cut in the basalt. Six hundred and four. Six hundred and nine. #still #line:0124395
Wall: Every year a different number. Births cut deep, deaths cut deeper. #still #line:039705d
Wall: One year the count falls by thirty-one. Nobody has smoothed the stone. #still #line:06c4ff3
===

title: PitHead_Cups
---
<<if has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein.walked")>>
    Table: Thirty-one cups by the boards, right side up, and clean. #still #line:05d1a7b
<<else>>
    Table: Thirty-one cups on a table by the boards, turned down. A name scratched in each one's glaze. #still #line:0243815
<<endif>>
===

title: Chimneys_Foot
---
Stone: Eight chimneys carry their builders' names, cut at the foot. #still #line:0aaf49b
Stone: This one's stone is bare. The soot on it is fresh. #still #line:0ea003a
===

title: Hollow_Lamps
---
Lamps: A hook for each miner, a lamp on each hook, a name plate under each lamp. #still #line:01e26e4
<<if has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein.walked")>>
    Lamps: Thirty-one lamps, lit. The families came down to light them. #still #line:033831e
<<else>>
    Lamps: Thirty-one hooks. Thirty-one plates. Nobody ever took the lamps down. #still #line:0c2481c
<<endif>>
===
